{
	title: 'Compact openable rows for queued messages',
	spec: 'A queued message waiting to run is local sticky state, not conversation. Terminal and web draw it at the transcript tail (task 2r) as a compact row with no card header and no blank lines inside: "(Queued at 15:29) text", or "(Queued at 15:29 by 76-cpo, tab 5) text" when another session queued it. The time is when its inbox record was written (InboxItem carries that ts). The tab is the sender\'s current tab number, redrawn when tabs change and omitted when it has none. Several waiting messages stack in run order. Each row folds like a tool card: closed, it shows at most 3 lines, then "… N more lines". Its id is the history line of its inbox record (task 9p), such as #u57, shown dim at the right on the terminal as an OSC 8 link to the web, where the card opens in full. The row gives no paused or blocked reason; the status line says why a session stalls. Steering and advisory messages keep the prompt card while waiting: steering waits only for cancelled work to settle. Once delivered, a queued message is a normal prompt card headed "10:53 You (queued)" or "10:53 Message from 76-cpo (queued)". titles.who builds every header as a sender plus a list of tags (steering, advisory, queued, command) rendered "who (a, b)", never as per-combination branches; a command the model issued is headed "Hal (command)". Tests make no assertions on label strings; they check that a message shows exactly once through the optimistic, waiting and delivered stages, and that queue origin survives a reload.',
	status: 'done',
